  "description": "Siskiyou: Conquer Rugged Terrain with Confidence\nThe Siskiyou is built to handle it all—whether you're bikepacking, exploring, or touring on rough, rugged terrain. With its 650b thru-axle wheels and adventure-ready geometry, this bike gives you the confidence to ride wherever the road (or trail) ends and the terrain gets tough.\nKey Features:\n\nOptimized for 650b or 27.5\" Wheels: Compatible with 45mm–55mm tires for superior traction on everything from gravel roads to rocky trails.\n\nReynolds 725 Steel Tubing: Rugged and durable, with an integrated chainstay yoke for added strength and performance.\n\nSteel Uni-Crown Touring Fork: Designed for stability, allowing precise handling even when fully loaded on rugged routes.\n\nProven Co-Motion Touring Geometry: Provides excellent stability and comfort on long, demanding rides across various terrains.\n\nRack, Fender, and Bottle Mounts: Equipped with the braze-ons needed for all your bikepacking gear, with three bottle mounts for ample hydration.\n\nMechanical Disc Brakes and Hand-Built Wheels: Reliable braking power and durable wheels that can take on any adventure.\n\nHandlebar Options:\n\nRoad drop bars for speed and efficiency\nMountain/trekking handlebars for maximum comfort on rough terrain\n\nThe Siskiyou is the bike you need when the road ends, and the adventure begins. Whether you're tackling steep hills or traversing rugged landscapes, this bike is built to keep you moving forward.\n\nClick here to get your Co-Motion Siskiyou order started!",
